# Datasets — far too large for GitHub (cs336/data/owt_sample/owt_train.txt alone is
# 11.4 GB).  GitHub hard-rejects files over 100 MB, so these stay local only.
#
# `**/data/*` matches the *contents* of any data/ directory at any depth rather than
# the directory itself.  That keeps the blanket protection identical to the previous
# `data/` rule, while letting an individual project opt a small sub-path back in —
# nlp-project tracks its dataset registry (sources, licences, commits, SHA-256)
# under data/manifests/.  Note `data/*` would NOT work here: a slash in the middle
# of a pattern anchors it to the repository root.
**/data/*
!**/data/manifests/

# Retired nested-repository metadata for cs336/assignment1-basics.
# Kept on disk as a backup of the stanford-cs336 upstream clone, never committed.
.git.upstream-backup/

# Python virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python caches / build output
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
